{title: He Leadeth Me}
{artist: Joseph H. Gilmore / William B. Bradbury}
{genre: Hymn, Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: F}
{tempo: 76}
{time: 4/4}
{score: he-leadeth-me.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]He leadeth me, O blessed thought!
O [Bb]words with [F]heavenly comfort [C]fraught
[F]Whate'er I do, where'er I be
Still [Bb]'tis God's [F]hand that [C]lead[F]eth me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[F]He leadeth me, He leadeth me
By His own [Bb]hand He [F]leadeth [C]me
His [F]faithful follower I would be
For [Bb]by His [F]hand He [C]lead[F]eth me
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Sometimes 'mid scenes of deepest gloom
Sometimes where [Bb]Eden's [F]bowers [C]bloom
[F]By waters still, o'er troubled sea
Still [Bb]'tis His [F]hand that [C]lead[F]eth me
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Lord, I would place my hand in Thine
Nor ever [Bb]murmur [F]nor re[C]pine
[F]Content, whatever lot I see
Since [Bb]'tis my [F]God that [C]lead[F]eth me
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]And when my task on earth is done
When by Thy [Bb]grace the [F]victory's [C]won
[F]E'en death's cold wave I will not flee
Since [Bb]God through [F]Jordan [C]lead[F]eth me
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
